   heterozygous. Default:0.95 
+- `--pair-aware`: Count DNA fragments instead of reads. Reads sharing
+  a name in one BAM file are one fragment across all peaks of a
+  chromosome and give at most one observation per position; mates
+  that disagree at a position are not counted there. In the SB
+  strand counts a fragment takes the strand of its first read in the
+  pair. `-D` and the
+  outlier filter still drop reads in each peak before the reads are
+  grouped. The depth fields (DP, DPT, DPC and the per-allele depths) count fragments
+  instead of reads. Heterozygous 0/1 calls on each chromosome are then
+  phased into phase blocks, across peaks: each call joins the nearest earlier call that the
+  treatment and control fragments spanning both link to it, so mates
+  can phase calls across the ones between them, and a fragment
+  whose reads fall in two peaks links calls in both. Default: off.
 
